WEBVTT

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:04.570
I've been considering naming him
after my husband.

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.333
It's been a tradition
in his family

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:09.240
for over five generations.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.539
I'm sure he'd be very pleased.

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:15.639
My husband's name is...
Greskrendtregk.

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.784
He's Ktarian.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:22.447
Choosing a name
is no easy matter.

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:24.354
I speak from experience.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:26.621
Have you had any progress,
Doctor?

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.895
I've reviewed
historical, literary

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:32.397
and anthropological databases
from over 500 worlds

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:35.299
and have yet to find
a suitable name.

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:37.667
However, I may want to
give some thought to...

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:40.639
Greskrendtregk.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:42.698
To be honest,

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:45.711
I've been thinking
of something simpler.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.645
What do you think of Cameron?

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.977
Oh, I like it.

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:50.778
Cameron... from the ancient

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:55.015
Celtic term
for "one whose nose is bent."

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:57.146
Well, what about Frederick?

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:59.488
Frederick.
Very distinguished.

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:02.290
However, it bears
a close resemblance

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:06.162
to a rather impolite term
on the Bolian homeworld.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:11.463
Well, it doesn't have to be
a human name.

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:13.096
I like Sural.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.606
It's Vulcan.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.165
Yes. Unfortunately,
it was also the name

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.836
of a dictator on Sakura Prime,

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:20.573
famed for beheading
his rivals...

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:22.513
and his parents.

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:24.608
He won't have an objection
to Benaren.

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:26.380
You're right. I've never heard
that name before.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:27.977
I think it's lovely.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.386
Is it Ocampan?

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:32.118
Benaren was my father's name.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.820
He was the greatest
inspiration in my life.

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:38.422
All science officers
please report to your stations.

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:40.399
Your scans look fine, Ensign.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:41.400
We'll see you in a week.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:42.696
Thank you.

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:46.467
Greskrendtregk would make

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.201
a good middle name,
don't you think?

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:54.808
You never suggested
your father's name to me.

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:58.443
I-I thought you were only
considering human names.

00:01:58.485 --> 00:02:01.784
Ah. Well, you were mistaken.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.288
If you like Benaren,

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:05.791
there's no reason
you can't use it, too.

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.656
I'm sure she won't mind.

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.958
Won't mind that I just
usurped her baby's name

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:11.291
the moment I heard it?

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:14.300
Thank you, but no, thank you.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.461
My uncle's name was Elrem.

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:18.937
I once knew a boy named Tarrik.

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:21.941
There's not much left
of whatever it was.

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:23.602
From the amount of debris,

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:26.976
I'd guess it was a small ship,
no bigger than a shuttlecraft.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:29.173
I'm not reading
any organic material

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.341
in the debris field.

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:31.816
It must have been
an unmanned vessel.

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:32.977
Possibly a probe.

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.452
Any idea what happened to it?

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.614
The high residual
energy signature

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:37.782
indicates repeated weapons fire.

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:40.418
Captain, the wreckage

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:43.190
is composed primarily
of duritanium polyalloy.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:45.431
Duritanium?

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:46.432
I haven't seen

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:48.366
many weapons that could
do that kind of damage

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:49.891
to a duritanium hull.

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:51.733
Transport some samples
of the debris

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:54.001
to Engineering for analysis.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.132
Continuous scans, Lieutenant.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:58.076
We don't want whoever did this
to catch us by surprise.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:07.443
Any conclusions?

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:08.954
Afraid so.

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:12.617
We've identified the signature
left by the weapons fire.

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:13.956
There's no question.

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.290
It was Cardassian.

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:16.795
Cardassian?

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.956
Could Seska be responsible?

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:22.968
No, Captain.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:24.536
I am.

00:05:13.812 --> 00:05:15.370
The probe was destroyed

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:17.644
by an experimental
Cardassian weapon

00:05:17.683 --> 00:05:19.344
from the Alpha Quadrant.

00:05:19.384 --> 00:05:21.875
Sorry.

00:05:22.721 --> 00:05:26.714
I recognized
its signature because...

00:05:26.758 --> 00:05:28.953
because I know
this weapon very well.

00:05:29.061 --> 00:05:30.460
Chakotay and I
got our hands on it

00:05:30.495 --> 00:05:32.520
when we were fighting
the Cardassians.

00:05:32.564 --> 00:05:34.293
How did it get here?

00:05:34.332 --> 00:05:36.163
Probably the same way we did.

00:05:36.201 --> 00:05:37.168
The last time we saw it,

00:05:37.202 --> 00:05:38.499
it was heading
in the same direction

00:05:38.537 --> 00:05:40.198
in the Badlands where
the Caretaker picked us up.

00:05:40.238 --> 00:05:41.637
Originally, the Cardassians

00:05:41.673 --> 00:05:44.904
sent this thing to destroy
a Maquis munitions base.

00:05:44.943 --> 00:05:46.638
We nicknamed it "Dreadnought."

00:05:46.678 --> 00:05:48.873
It's a self-guided
tactical missile

00:05:48.914 --> 00:05:51.576
carrying a charge
of a thousand kilos of matter

00:05:51.616 --> 00:05:53.948
and another thousand
of antimatter.

00:05:53.985 --> 00:05:56.180
Enough to destroy
a small moon.

00:05:56.221 --> 00:05:57.688
Now, add to that

00:05:57.723 --> 00:06:02.023
one of the most sophisticated
computer systems I've ever seen.

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:04.551
They made this missile
adaptable, evasive,

00:06:04.596 --> 00:06:06.928
armed with its own
defensive weaponry...

00:06:06.965 --> 00:06:09.593
in other words, unstoppable.

00:06:09.634 --> 00:06:12.467
So, how did you stop it?

00:06:12.504 --> 00:06:15.132
We didn't.
It got through all our defenses.

00:06:15.173 --> 00:06:18.506
Worked like it was supposed to,
except for one minor detail.

00:06:18.543 --> 00:06:19.942
It didn't go off.

00:06:20.045 --> 00:06:21.569
Leave it to the Cardassians
to build

00:06:21.613 --> 00:06:23.638
such an incredibly advanced
tactical weapon

00:06:23.682 --> 00:06:26.879
and then arm the warhead
with an old kinetic detonator.

00:06:26.918 --> 00:06:28.943
The missile skipped off
into the atmosphere

00:06:28.987 --> 00:06:30.784
and quietly went into orbit.

00:06:30.822 --> 00:06:34.918
I got inside it
and reprogrammed the computer.

00:06:36.828 --> 00:06:38.386
Hell, I didn't
just reprogram it,

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:40.295
I changed its identity.

00:06:40.332 --> 00:06:42.459
I made it forget
about being Cardassian.

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:44.128
Now it was working
for the Maquis.

00:06:44.169 --> 00:06:45.966
And we gave it a new mission...

00:06:46.071 --> 00:06:47.939
to destroy the Cardassian
fuel depot on Aschelan V.

00:06:47.939 --> 00:06:49.270
To destroy the Cardassian
fuel depot on Aschelan V.

00:06:49.307 --> 00:06:51.275
But it never made it
out of the Badlands.

00:06:51.309 --> 00:06:53.777
We thought it had been destroyed
in one of the plasma storms.

00:06:53.811 --> 00:06:55.108
So, how do we

00:06:55.146 --> 00:06:57.876
stop this weapon before
it causes any more damage?

00:06:57.915 --> 00:06:59.883
Dreadnought masks its warp trail

00:06:59.917 --> 00:07:02.351
with a randomized EM field,
but I can modify

00:07:02.386 --> 00:07:04.752
our navigational sensors
to cut through that.

00:07:04.789 --> 00:07:06.916
And what are going we do with it
once we find it?

00:07:06.958 --> 00:07:08.448
I get back inside it.

00:07:08.492 --> 00:07:10.653
I know all the security codes.

00:07:10.695 --> 00:07:12.458
I installed them myself.

00:07:12.496 --> 00:07:14.123
Lieutenant Paris
can assist you

00:07:14.165 --> 00:07:16.133
with the navigational sensors.

00:07:16.167 --> 00:07:17.566
Keep me informed.

00:07:17.601 --> 00:07:19.159
Dismissed.

00:07:21.339 --> 00:07:25.139
Lieutenant? I expect everyone
to show up for meetings on time

00:07:25.176 --> 00:07:26.734
and properly dressed.

00:07:31.248 --> 00:07:32.840
Yes, sir.

00:07:38.055 --> 00:07:40.649
There's still
a lot of distortion

00:07:40.691 --> 00:07:42.318
in the upper frequencies.

00:07:43.561 --> 00:07:47.156
Better.
Now let's try filtering out

00:07:47.198 --> 00:07:48.290
the ion radiation.

00:07:52.003 --> 00:07:53.698
B'Elanna.

00:07:58.676 --> 00:08:02.237
You must be really worried
about catching this thing.

00:08:03.981 --> 00:08:07.246
Chakotay wasn't telling
the whole truth.

00:08:07.284 --> 00:08:08.911
We didn't send Dreadnought

00:08:08.986 --> 00:08:11.284
on a mission
against the Cardassians.

00:08:11.322 --> 00:08:14.621
I was the one who sent it...

00:08:14.658 --> 00:08:17.286
without asking him.

00:08:17.328 --> 00:08:19.319
You were afraid he'd say no.

00:08:25.269 --> 00:08:28.033
After I did it,
he pulled me aside, and...

00:08:28.072 --> 00:08:30.233
I was ready to defend myself.

00:08:30.274 --> 00:08:32.868
I was so sure
that I had anticipated

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:35.674
everything that could
possibly go wrong.

00:08:35.713 --> 00:08:37.271
I even programmed it

00:08:37.314 --> 00:08:40.306
to warn Federation ships
to stay out of its way.

00:08:40.351 --> 00:08:41.648
In my own voice.

00:08:41.685 --> 00:08:43.118
Your voice.

00:08:43.154 --> 00:08:46.612
Listening to that Cardassian
computer's voice

00:08:46.657 --> 00:08:48.249
was driving me crazy.

00:08:48.292 --> 00:08:50.283
I don't blame you.

00:08:50.327 --> 00:08:54.423
Anyway, Chakotay looked at me...

00:08:54.465 --> 00:08:57.662
I didn't know him
very well yet...

00:08:57.701 --> 00:09:05.164
and all he said in that
damned soft voice of his was...

00:09:05.209 --> 00:09:08.667
that I'd hurt him.

00:09:08.712 --> 00:09:13.706
That he thought he'd earned
my trust and loyalty.

00:09:13.751 --> 00:09:17.016
I was so glad
when it disappeared

00:09:17.054 --> 00:09:18.351
into the Badlands.

00:09:18.389 --> 00:09:21.517
I remember thinking,
"Thank God it's over."

00:09:23.494 --> 00:09:26.088
But it's not.

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:31.625
And if anything happens here
because of Dreadnought...

00:09:31.669 --> 00:09:33.466
it's my fault.

00:09:33.504 --> 00:09:36.098
No one else's.

00:09:38.142 --> 00:09:40.042
You took a risk.

00:09:40.077 --> 00:09:42.238
You were thinking like a Maquis.

00:09:42.279 --> 00:09:44.770
That was a whole different life.

00:09:44.815 --> 00:09:47.443
Tell me about it.

00:09:47.485 --> 00:09:49.476
You know...

00:09:51.188 --> 00:09:52.348
I've been surprised

00:09:52.389 --> 00:09:54.016
at how well you've been
able to fit in here.

00:09:56.127 --> 00:09:58.687
A little envious, too.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:05.728
Tom...

00:10:05.769 --> 00:10:08.431
what's been going on
with you lately?

00:10:08.472 --> 00:10:10.565
Going on? How?

00:10:10.608 --> 00:10:13.736
People are starting to talk.

00:10:13.777 --> 00:10:15.335
Are they?

00:10:15.379 --> 00:10:17.142
People like who? Chakotay?

00:10:17.181 --> 00:10:18.478
No, I mean people

00:10:18.516 --> 00:10:20.507
like me.

00:10:20.551 --> 00:10:22.178
Like today.

00:10:22.219 --> 00:10:23.618
Look at yourself.

00:10:23.654 --> 00:10:26.487
Coming to a briefing late

00:10:26.524 --> 00:10:28.116
and is it true

00:10:28.159 --> 00:10:30.650
that you had a fight
with Lieutenant Rollins?

00:10:32.196 --> 00:10:34.255
The Lieutenant was unhappy

00:10:34.298 --> 00:10:36.823
that my Conn reports
weren't punctuated properly...

00:10:36.867 --> 00:10:39.427
according to Starfleet protocol.

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:41.802
I didn't like his attitude.

00:10:41.839 --> 00:10:43.864
Was he right about your reports?

00:10:43.908 --> 00:10:46.968
We're in the Delta Quadrant;
nowhere near Starfleet.

00:10:47.011 --> 00:10:48.342
What differe?

00:10:53.284 --> 00:10:56.617
Yeah, he was right.

00:10:56.654 --> 00:10:58.952
I'm the one who's been wrong.

00:10:58.989 --> 00:11:02.288
Wrong about a lot of things.

00:11:04.695 --> 00:11:07.687
Why don't we try running
a multiphasic sweep?

00:11:15.806 --> 00:11:17.967
Captain, I'm picking up
the trail again.

00:11:18.075 --> 00:11:19.667
New heading: 196 mark 4.

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:20.972
I'm on it.

00:11:21.045 --> 00:11:22.512
This course is erratic.

00:11:22.546 --> 00:11:25.174
Are we sure we're following
a single warp trail?

00:11:25.216 --> 00:11:26.649
Perhaps the missile's
navigational system

00:11:26.684 --> 00:11:27.981
is malfunctioning.

00:11:28.018 --> 00:11:29.645
It's been operating
for over a year...

00:11:29.687 --> 00:11:31.416
far longer than it was
designed to function.

00:11:31.455 --> 00:11:32.922
No. This is deliberate.

00:11:32.957 --> 00:11:34.686
It's following one
of the evasive patterns

00:11:34.725 --> 00:11:36.158
I programmed into it.

00:11:36.193 --> 00:11:38.093
It must have observed us
following.

00:11:38.128 --> 00:11:41.586
I think I've got it
on long-range sensors.

00:11:41.632 --> 00:11:43.156
No, that's only a sensor echo.

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:45.498
Dreadnought's programmed
to deflect its image

00:11:45.536 --> 00:11:48.004
up to 100,000 kilometers
from its true location.

00:11:48.038 --> 00:11:49.665
The next time you get a heading,

00:11:49.707 --> 00:11:51.971
look for a brief surge
in neutrino emissions

00:11:52.009 --> 00:11:53.909
within 100,000-kilometer radius.

00:11:53.944 --> 00:11:55.468
That'll be the real thing.

00:11:57.314 --> 00:11:58.872
Got it.

00:11:58.916 --> 00:12:00.611
Elevated neutrino levels.

00:12:00.651 --> 00:12:02.118
Locking in coordinates.

00:12:02.152 --> 00:12:03.710
It's within visual range.

00:12:03.754 --> 00:12:05.381
On screen.

00:12:15.499 --> 00:12:18.297
Its targeting scanners
have been activated.

00:12:18.335 --> 00:12:20.064
What's wrong?

00:12:20.104 --> 00:12:21.935
It's not supposed to do that

00:12:21.972 --> 00:12:24.463
until it's locked
onto its final target.

00:12:26.610 --> 00:12:28.339
It's heading for a planet

00:12:28.379 --> 00:12:30.973
in a system
over ten light-years away.

00:12:31.015 --> 00:12:32.983
At its current speed,

00:12:33.050 --> 00:12:35.644
it'll get there
in about three weeks.

00:12:35.686 --> 00:12:37.517
The planet is Class-M.

00:12:37.554 --> 00:12:41.456
I'm reading several
heavily-populated areas.

00:12:52.102 --> 00:12:53.626
Seska will want to know

00:12:53.671 --> 00:12:56.196
about this Cardassian missile
immediately.

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:59.971
Mr. Jonas,
your enthusiasm is appreciated,

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:03.241
but I would prefer
to know more about it

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:04.941
before I bring it
to Maje Culluh's attention.

00:13:05.049 --> 00:13:08.075
If I could just talk to Seska.

00:13:08.118 --> 00:13:13.215
As I explained, I have now been
assigned to be your control.

00:13:13.257 --> 00:13:16.283
Look, has she been made aware of
how much I've been helping you?

00:13:16.327 --> 00:13:20.320
What the maje chooses to share
with her is none of my concern,

00:13:20.364 --> 00:13:23.527
but you are in good hands,
my friend.

00:13:23.567 --> 00:13:26.593
Now, tell me more about
this weapon your ship has found.

00:13:26.637 --> 00:13:30.164
Look, all you need to tell Seska
is that missile is better armed

00:13:30.207 --> 00:13:32.141
than the entire
Kazon-Nistrim sect.

00:13:32.176 --> 00:13:34.201
That's very interesting.

00:13:34.244 --> 00:13:35.973
What more can you tell me
that I can bring to my?

00:13:36.046 --> 00:13:38.674
Someone's about to make
a subspace transmission.

00:13:38.716 --> 00:13:41.480
They may be able
to detect our com-link.

00:13:41.518 --> 00:13:43.577
I have to terminate.

00:13:46.757 --> 00:13:48.349
My name is Kathryn Janeway,

00:13:48.392 --> 00:13:50.792
Captain of
the Federation Starship Voyager.

00:13:50.828 --> 00:13:52.796
First Minister Kellan, Captain.

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:54.398
What is it you want?

00:13:54.531 --> 00:13:55.998
Our scans of your world

00:13:56.066 --> 00:13:58.728
suggest you have
long-range tracking abilities.

00:13:58.769 --> 00:14:01.932
We have been observing your
course for the last two days.

00:14:02.005 --> 00:14:04.064
Have you also been able
to detect the missile

00:14:04.107 --> 00:14:06.098
on a parallel course
off our starboard bow?

00:14:06.143 --> 00:14:11.581
We haven't been able to identify
what it is, but yes.

00:14:13.083 --> 00:14:15.210
You have the right to know,
First Minister,

00:14:15.252 --> 00:14:16.583
that this missile
is carrying a warhead

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:18.815
with a significant
destructive force, and...

00:14:18.855 --> 00:14:21.187
Is this some sort of threat,
Captain?

00:14:21.224 --> 00:14:22.521
On the contrary.

00:14:22.559 --> 00:14:23.856
We want to help.

00:14:23.894 --> 00:14:25.657
I find that hard to believe.

00:14:25.695 --> 00:14:27.754
Your reputation
precedes you, Captain.

00:14:27.798 --> 00:14:30.631
We've been told that you've
threatened many races

00:14:30.667 --> 00:14:32.760
since your arrival
in this Quadrant.

00:14:32.803 --> 00:14:34.634
First Minister, we're aware

00:14:34.671 --> 00:14:36.969
the Kazon have been
telling that to people.

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:39.508
They'd like to prevent us
from making allies.

00:14:39.543 --> 00:14:41.408
I assure you,
you've been misled.

00:14:41.445 --> 00:14:45.506
And yet, here you are,
sending this missile toward us.

00:14:45.549 --> 00:14:47.642
The missile arrived here
from our Quadrant

00:14:47.684 --> 00:14:49.584
due to a very unusual accident.

00:14:49.619 --> 00:14:51.416
We haven't been able
to determine yet

00:14:51.455 --> 00:14:53.218
why it chose Rakosa
as its target,

00:14:53.256 --> 00:14:54.723
but my Chief Engineer

00:14:54.758 --> 00:14:57.226
is preparing to disarm it
before it reaches you.

00:14:57.260 --> 00:15:01.128
Perhaps you are telling me this
in order to delay

00:15:01.164 --> 00:15:02.859
our defensive response.

00:15:02.899 --> 00:15:05.527
I could've maintained
communication silence

00:15:05.569 --> 00:15:07.901
and not given you
any warning at all.

00:15:07.938 --> 00:15:09.235
That's true.

00:15:09.272 --> 00:15:10.899
Nevertheless,

00:15:10.941 --> 00:15:14.775
be aware that I am placing
our defense force on alert.

00:15:14.811 --> 00:15:17.507
I'd do the same, in your place.

00:15:17.547 --> 00:15:20.744
We will be watching
your progress closely.

00:15:23.086 --> 00:15:25.179
Janeway to Torres.

00:15:25.222 --> 00:15:27.554
How soon will you be ready
to transport?

00:15:27.591 --> 00:15:29.957
Dreadnought's shields
have responded to my codes.

00:15:30.026 --> 00:15:31.357
I'm ready now, Captain.

00:15:31.394 --> 00:15:32.361
Proceed.

00:15:32.395 --> 00:15:33.384
Energize.

00:15:39.836 --> 00:15:41.895
Authorized entry detected.

00:15:41.938 --> 00:15:43.462
Initiating DNA scan.

00:15:43.507 --> 00:15:46.203
B'Elanna Torres confirmed.

00:15:46.243 --> 00:15:47.870
Hello, B'Elanna.

00:15:47.911 --> 00:15:51.608
Your last systems access
was on stardate 47582.

00:15:51.648 --> 00:15:53.946
Current date is 49447.

00:15:53.984 --> 00:15:56.316
Time: 0840 hours.

00:15:56.353 --> 00:15:59.117
Did you sleep well last night?

00:15:59.155 --> 00:16:01.419
Not so well,
to tell you the truth.

00:16:01.458 --> 00:16:03.449
Activate programmer interface.

00:16:03.493 --> 00:16:05.654
Your presence
was not anticipated

00:16:05.695 --> 00:16:08.163
during the mission.
Please explain.

00:16:08.198 --> 00:16:11.395
Something's gone wrong with
your programming, Dreadnought.

00:16:13.336 --> 00:16:15.361
Display targeting schematic.

00:16:15.405 --> 00:16:18.806
A self-diagnostic has been
conducted every 14 hours.

00:16:18.842 --> 00:16:21.140
No malfunctions
have been detected.

00:16:21.177 --> 00:16:23.168
Maybe there's something wrong

00:16:23.213 --> 00:16:25.147
with your diagnostic
systems, too.

00:16:25.181 --> 00:16:26.648
Identify target.

00:16:26.683 --> 00:16:29.413
Aschelan V.

00:16:29.452 --> 00:16:31.943
What targeting parameters
are you using?

00:16:32.055 --> 00:16:34.956
Size, radiothermic signature,

00:16:34.991 --> 00:16:37.255
atmospheric composition,
relative...

00:16:37.294 --> 00:16:38.488
Enough.

00:16:38.528 --> 00:16:40.962
Dreadnought, you're nowhere near
Aschelan V.

00:16:41.031 --> 00:16:45.297
Based on available data,
you are mistaken, B'Elanna.

00:16:45.335 --> 00:16:48.771
Let me check out
your navigational systems.

00:16:48.805 --> 00:16:50.397
Access to primary
navigational systems

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:53.898
is denied
at stage three alert status.

00:16:53.944 --> 00:16:55.844
That was my idea, wasn't it?

00:16:55.879 --> 00:16:57.403
Affirmative.

00:16:57.447 --> 00:16:59.972
Okay. We'll have to go at this

00:17:00.016 --> 00:17:01.881
in a different way then,
won't we?

00:17:12.829 --> 00:17:16.629
Dreadnought,
do you know what happened to you

00:17:16.666 --> 00:17:19.829
the day after
my last systems access?

00:17:19.869 --> 00:17:21.700
Please be more specific.

00:17:21.738 --> 00:17:25.105
Did you encounter
a coherent tetryon beam?

00:17:25.141 --> 00:17:26.608
Confirmed.

00:17:26.643 --> 00:17:29.510
All attempts
to avoid the phenomenon failed.

00:17:29.546 --> 00:17:32.606
That beam carried you
into the Delta Quadrant.

00:17:32.649 --> 00:17:35.516
I'm not surprised
it damaged your sensors.

00:17:40.423 --> 00:17:44.723
Dreadnought, reinitialize
your navigational systems.

00:17:44.761 --> 00:17:46.592
Computer?

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:48.962
Reinitialization sequence
is complete.

00:17:48.999 --> 00:17:51.524
Okay.

00:17:51.568 --> 00:17:54.969
Now verify our current position.

00:17:55.005 --> 00:17:59.101
Based on relative position
to known astronomical markers,

00:17:59.142 --> 00:18:02.441
this vessel is currently located
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:18:02.479 --> 00:18:05.778
And is Aschelan V
located in the Delta Quadrant?

00:18:05.815 --> 00:18:07.442
Negative.

00:18:07.484 --> 00:18:09.782
Then reconfirm your target lock.

00:18:09.819 --> 00:18:11.116
Unable to verify.

00:18:11.154 --> 00:18:13.486
Standing down from stage three.

00:18:13.523 --> 00:18:15.684
Target lock
has been deactivated.

00:18:15.725 --> 00:18:19.491
Reestablishing stage four.

00:18:19.529 --> 00:18:20.791
Janeway to Torres.

00:18:20.830 --> 00:18:21.922
Go ahead, Captain.

00:18:21.965 --> 00:18:23.865
We're showing a shutdown
of all your engines.

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:25.595
Can you confirm that?

00:18:25.635 --> 00:18:27.102
That and more.

00:18:27.137 --> 00:18:28.798
I'll be ready to transport back
in a few minutes.

00:18:28.838 --> 00:18:29.805
Acknowledged.

00:18:29.839 --> 00:18:30.806
Good work, B'Elanna.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:31.932
Janeway out.

00:18:34.711 --> 00:18:37.441
Dreadnought,
return to stage five.

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:40.813
Initiate powersave program.

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:41.942
Acknowledged.

00:18:42.018 --> 00:18:43.349
Good night, B'Elanna.

00:18:43.386 --> 00:18:45.752
Sweet dreams.

00:18:49.292 --> 00:18:50.589
The Dreadnought's
quantum torpedoes

00:18:50.627 --> 00:18:51.958
could be modified
to be compatible

00:18:52.028 --> 00:18:53.052
with our launchers.

00:18:53.096 --> 00:18:54.529
What about
its engine components?

00:18:54.564 --> 00:18:56.555
Easily converted
to Starfleet specs.

00:18:56.599 --> 00:18:57.964
We'll have spare parts
for years.

00:18:58.001 --> 00:18:59.525
We should also
download some files

00:18:59.569 --> 00:19:01.002
from the computer core.

00:19:01.037 --> 00:19:02.834
B'Elanna, you can begin
the salvage operation

00:19:02.872 --> 00:19:04.066
first thing in the...

00:19:04.107 --> 00:19:05.404
Paris to Janeway.

00:19:05.442 --> 00:19:06.739
Yes, Lieutenant?

00:19:06.776 --> 00:19:08.471
The missile just took off.
It's going into warp.

00:19:08.511 --> 00:19:10.502
Stay with it, Tom.

00:19:12.348 --> 00:19:13.815
Engaging warp drive.

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:14.874
This is impossible.

00:19:14.918 --> 00:19:16.783
When I left,
it was completely shut down.

00:19:18.688 --> 00:19:20.918
We're back on a heading
to Rakosa V.

00:19:21.024 --> 00:19:23.652
It's increasing speed to warp 9.

00:19:23.693 --> 00:19:26.685
At this rate, it'll reach
the planet in 51 hours.

00:19:38.341 --> 00:19:40.639
It's still on course
for the planet at warp 9.

00:19:40.677 --> 00:19:43.202
Mr. Paris, bring us
within ten kilometers.

00:19:43.246 --> 00:19:44.770
Maintain a parallel position.

00:19:44.814 --> 00:19:46.145
Bridge to Torres.
Your status?

00:19:46.182 --> 00:19:47.581
I don't understand it, Captain.

00:19:47.617 --> 00:19:49.676
Dreadnought's shields
are not recognizing

00:19:49.719 --> 00:19:51.084
my security code anymore.

00:19:51.121 --> 00:19:52.816
We can't initiate transport.

00:19:52.856 --> 00:19:54.551
You better get back up here,
Lieutenant.

00:19:57.193 --> 00:19:58.182
Aye, Captain.

00:20:00.897 --> 00:20:04.526
Mr. Tuvok, let's take a shot
at disabling its drive systems.

00:20:04.567 --> 00:20:06.296
Ready photons. Red Alert.

00:20:06.336 --> 00:20:08.497
Torres programmed
the missile's shields

00:20:08.538 --> 00:20:11.268
to adjust to all known
weapons, even Starfleet's.

00:20:11.307 --> 00:20:13.502
Voyager wasn't in service
when she did it.

00:20:13.543 --> 00:20:15.977
We're equipped
with type-6 photon torpedoes.

00:20:16.012 --> 00:20:17.138
They may just get through.

00:20:17.180 --> 00:20:18.169
Fire.

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:25.745
No discernible damage, Captain.

00:20:25.789 --> 00:20:29.190
It must have scanned our
weapons, adapted its shields.

00:20:29.225 --> 00:20:32.295
Captain, it's maintaining
course and speed.

00:20:32.428 --> 00:20:34.862
We're being hailed
by the missile.

00:20:34.897 --> 00:20:36.990
Let's hear it.

00:20:37.099 --> 00:20:40.330
Unidentified Federation ship.

00:20:40.369 --> 00:20:43.634
Although this vessel
is Cardassian in design,

00:20:43.673 --> 00:20:46.164
it has been appropriated
by the Maquis.

00:20:46.208 --> 00:20:48.176
Please stand down your weapons.

00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:51.646
You stand down your weapons
and I'll stand down mine.

00:20:51.681 --> 00:20:54.013
You are interfering
with a tactical mission

00:20:54.083 --> 00:20:55.880
against Cardassian aggressors.

00:20:55.918 --> 00:20:57.545
This vessel is programmed

00:20:57.586 --> 00:20:59.918
to respond
with all necessary force

00:20:59.955 --> 00:21:03.118
to prevent any disruption
to its mission.

00:21:03.159 --> 00:21:05.855
Dreadnought,
why have you resumed course?

00:21:05.895 --> 00:21:07.294
Hello, B'Elanna.

00:21:07.330 --> 00:21:09.059
Course was resumed

00:21:09.098 --> 00:21:12.090
once your safe departure
from this vessel was confirmed.

00:21:12.134 --> 00:21:15.968
It was a necessary response
to your deception.

00:21:16.038 --> 00:21:17.972
My "deception"?!

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:21.237
You are participating
in the Delta Quadrant deception.

00:21:21.277 --> 00:21:22.642
Explain, Dreadnought.

00:21:22.678 --> 00:21:25.146
False information
has been entered

00:21:25.181 --> 00:21:28.446
into Dreadnought's
navigational sensor array.

00:21:28.484 --> 00:21:30.816
When a bomb starts
talking about itself

00:21:30.853 --> 00:21:32.912
in the third person,
I get worried.

00:21:32.955 --> 00:21:35.788
Why would I enter
false information?

00:21:35.825 --> 00:21:37.986
Probability assessment indicates

00:21:38.060 --> 00:21:40.824
you are being coerced
by Cardassian forces.

00:21:40.863 --> 00:21:42.728
You've already
identified Voyager

00:21:42.765 --> 00:21:44.630
as a Federation ship,
Dreadnought.

00:21:44.667 --> 00:21:46.225
Your scanners must indicate

00:21:46.268 --> 00:21:47.929
this is not
a Cardassian crew.

00:21:47.970 --> 00:21:49.995
Probability assessment indicates

00:21:50.106 --> 00:21:52.540
you are operating
within the parameters

00:21:52.575 --> 00:21:54.236
of the Cardassian-Federation
Alliance,

00:21:54.276 --> 00:21:57.575
as described
in the Treaty of 2367,

00:21:57.613 --> 00:21:59.877
a treaty rejected by the Maquis.

00:21:59.915 --> 00:22:03.214
So when I was just over there
and you shut yourself off,

00:22:03.252 --> 00:22:04.412
you were lying to me?

00:22:04.453 --> 00:22:05.750
Acknowledged.

00:22:07.289 --> 00:22:09.780
I never taught it to do that.

00:22:09.825 --> 00:22:11.793
That is not correct, B'Elanna.

00:22:11.827 --> 00:22:14.455
Your tactical subroutine
instructed Dreadnought

00:22:14.497 --> 00:22:18.126
to prepare responses for 39
potential Cardassian threats.

00:22:18.167 --> 00:22:22.194
The possibility of your capture
and coercion was number seven.

00:22:22.238 --> 00:22:25.230
Dreadnought, is there any way
we can prove to you

00:22:25.274 --> 00:22:27.572
that you are actually
in the Delta Quadrant;

00:22:27.610 --> 00:22:29.305
that this is not a deception?

00:22:29.345 --> 00:22:32.143
The probability of being
in the Delta Quadrant,

00:22:32.181 --> 00:22:35.150
75,000 light-years
from last confirmed location,

00:22:35.184 --> 00:22:36.617
is negligible.

00:22:36.652 --> 00:22:39.485
The target is located
in the Alpha Quadrant.

00:22:39.522 --> 00:22:41.752
Target lock has been
established.

00:22:41.791 --> 00:22:43.986
There will be
no further warnings.

00:22:44.026 --> 00:22:46.517
Terminating communications link.

00:22:52.134 --> 00:22:56.093
The one possible vulnerability
I remember

00:22:56.138 --> 00:22:59.107
is in the thoron shock emitter.

00:22:59.141 --> 00:23:02.406
If we can get it
to fire at full power,

00:23:02.445 --> 00:23:05.608
that should destabilize
the reactor core for 30 seconds.

00:23:05.648 --> 00:23:07.741
A single sustained tachyon beam

00:23:07.783 --> 00:23:10.217
might just penetrate that core
and destroy it.

00:23:10.252 --> 00:23:13.119
What will it take to provoke
Dreadnought into firing?

00:23:13.155 --> 00:23:14.349
It shouldn't be that difficult.

00:23:14.390 --> 00:23:15.948
Once we go after it
with an all-out assault,

00:23:15.991 --> 00:23:16.958
the emitter should fire.

00:23:16.992 --> 00:23:19.825
Mr. Tuvok, set your target.

00:23:21.030 --> 00:23:23.328
Ready photons.

00:23:23.365 --> 00:23:24.957
Ready, Captain.

00:23:25.067 --> 00:23:27.399
Fire.

00:23:32.942 --> 00:23:35.809
The missile's
thoron shock emitter has fired.

00:23:36.812 --> 00:23:38.370
Initiate the tachyon beam.

00:23:43.586 --> 00:23:45.417
We have penetrated its shields.

00:23:45.454 --> 00:23:46.819
Direct hit to the core.

00:23:46.856 --> 00:23:49.586
Reading an energy
buildup in its reactor.

00:23:49.625 --> 00:23:51.991
It should overload
in about 30 seconds.

00:23:52.094 --> 00:23:53.425
Wait a minute.

00:23:53.462 --> 00:23:56.431
There's a plasma surge
coming from its core.

00:23:56.465 --> 00:23:58.399
What the hell?

00:24:08.410 --> 00:24:09.604
Report!

00:24:09.645 --> 00:24:12.113
It sent a plasma burst
along the tachyon beam

00:24:12.147 --> 00:24:13.739
into our main power system.

00:24:13.782 --> 00:24:16.046
We've got EPS relays
burned out all over the ship.

00:24:16.085 --> 00:24:18.952
I'm not getting any response
from the warp or impulse drives.

00:24:19.021 --> 00:24:22.388
Even the maneuvering thrusters
are out!

00:24:22.424 --> 00:24:24.187
The missile was not
significantly damaged.

00:24:24.226 --> 00:24:26.558
It has maintained
its course for Rakosa.

00:24:35.437 --> 00:24:36.961
Our engines will be back on line

00:24:37.039 --> 00:24:38.631
in less than an hour,
First Minister.

00:24:38.674 --> 00:24:39.800
Then we'll try again.

00:24:39.842 --> 00:24:42.174
Did you sustain
any casualties, Captain?

00:24:42.211 --> 00:24:43.508
A few.

00:24:43.546 --> 00:24:45.138
A broken arm, a broken leg.

00:24:45.180 --> 00:24:46.807
Fortunately, that's all.

00:24:46.849 --> 00:24:48.578
I'm pleased to hear that.

00:24:48.617 --> 00:24:51.313
We are projecting casualties
at two million,

00:24:51.353 --> 00:24:52.650
if the worst occurs.

00:24:52.688 --> 00:24:56.089
I have deployed our fleet
to intercept this missile

00:24:56.125 --> 00:24:57.592
in a matter of hours.

00:24:57.626 --> 00:25:01.528
First Minister, we've analyzed
your offensive capabilities...

00:25:01.564 --> 00:25:04.362
and they're no match
for what you're facing.

00:25:04.400 --> 00:25:06.766
You must have realized that
yourself.

00:25:06.802 --> 00:25:08.565
And what would you have me do,

00:25:08.604 --> 00:25:12.506
sit here and wait for death
to fall from the sky?

00:25:15.477 --> 00:25:17.274
I'm sorry.

00:25:17.313 --> 00:25:19.144
We haven't had much sleep.

00:25:21.216 --> 00:25:23.207
We weren't prepared
for anything like this.

00:25:23.252 --> 00:25:24.947
We are not a warlike race.

00:25:24.987 --> 00:25:26.284
We haven't devoted

00:25:26.322 --> 00:25:29.382
our resources to building
weapons like yours.

00:25:29.425 --> 00:25:30.449
First Minister...

00:25:30.492 --> 00:25:31.618
Please.

00:25:31.660 --> 00:25:34.458
I've always hated that title.

00:25:34.496 --> 00:25:36.555
My name is Kellan.

00:25:36.599 --> 00:25:37.930
I prefer that.

00:25:37.967 --> 00:25:39.059
Our Chief Engineer

00:25:39.101 --> 00:25:41.331
is trying to return
to the missile's control room.

00:25:41.370 --> 00:25:43.395
She's still our best chance
at disarming it.

00:25:43.439 --> 00:25:46.966
There's no reason to send your
fleet on a hopeless mission.

00:25:47.042 --> 00:25:50.068
I appreciate your efforts,
truly,

00:25:50.112 --> 00:25:53.081
but the decision has been made.

00:25:53.115 --> 00:25:55.276
We have some good pilots,
Captain.

00:25:55.317 --> 00:25:57.478
Perhaps they will surprise you.

00:26:05.961 --> 00:26:07.121
Blocked again.

00:26:09.365 --> 00:26:11.265
We don't have time for this.

00:26:11.300 --> 00:26:13.666
Don't worry, we'll find a way
to get you back over there.

00:26:13.702 --> 00:26:14.930
We wouldn't have to

00:26:14.970 --> 00:26:16.631
if I'd done my job right
the first time.

00:26:16.672 --> 00:26:18.765
You couldn't expect to
guess every move it made.

00:26:18.807 --> 00:26:20.798
Why not? Dreadnought seems
pretty good at guessing mine.

00:26:20.843 --> 00:26:22.868
It's only as smart
as you made it.

00:26:22.911 --> 00:26:24.344
I'm not so sure about that,
Harry.

00:26:24.380 --> 00:26:26.177
Its programs are adaptive

00:26:26.215 --> 00:26:28.410
and it's been accumulating data
all this time.

00:26:28.450 --> 00:26:30.145
It spends every minute
of every day

00:26:30.185 --> 00:26:32.346
thinking about new strategies,
new probabilities.

00:26:32.388 --> 00:26:34.151
And I bet it doesn't
spend much time

00:26:34.189 --> 00:26:36.555
worrying about what it
could have done differently.

00:26:41.530 --> 00:26:43.930
All right, Starfleet...

00:26:43.966 --> 00:26:45.490
let's give it another try.

00:27:03.585 --> 00:27:06.418
Unauthorized entry detected.

00:27:06.455 --> 00:27:08.446
Initiating DNA scan.

00:27:09.692 --> 00:27:11.284
Hello, B'Elanna.

00:27:11.326 --> 00:27:15.922
Your last systems access
was today at 0840 hours.

00:27:15.964 --> 00:27:18.330
Current time is 1931 hours.

00:27:18.367 --> 00:27:19.732
Have you had a pleasant day?

00:27:19.768 --> 00:27:22.134
Oh, yeah. Swell day.

00:27:22.171 --> 00:27:25.140
Access to programmer interface
has been denied.

00:27:28.243 --> 00:27:31.576
Access to programmer interface
has been denied.

00:27:45.592 --> 00:27:50.461
Access to circuit pathways
has been denied.

00:27:50.497 --> 00:27:53.364
Be advised that the intensity
of the shock will increase

00:27:53.400 --> 00:27:55.664
if you attempt to open
the panel again.

00:28:12.652 --> 00:28:15.416
I'm disappointed in you,
Dreadnought.

00:28:15.455 --> 00:28:19.221
If I really was
a Cardassian agent...

00:28:19.259 --> 00:28:21.853
you should've killed me
with the first charge.

00:28:21.895 --> 00:28:25.422
Probability assessment indicates
that you are being coerced

00:28:25.465 --> 00:28:27.456
by Cardassian forces.

00:28:37.744 --> 00:28:40.770
Somehow I expected you
to put up more of a fight.

00:28:42.816 --> 00:28:44.147
Computer?

00:28:46.519 --> 00:28:48.919
Stage two alert
has been activated.

00:28:48.955 --> 00:28:50.718
Tell me what's happening.

00:28:50.757 --> 00:28:53.555
There are 15 priority targets
approaching.

00:28:53.593 --> 00:28:56.255
All weapon systems
at full readiness.

00:28:56.296 --> 00:28:58.389
Speed: Full impulse.

00:28:58.431 --> 00:29:00.661
The Rakosan fleet.

00:29:08.608 --> 00:29:10.235
Hail the lead ship.

00:29:10.276 --> 00:29:12.335
Channel open, Captain.

00:29:12.379 --> 00:29:13.869
Audio only.

00:29:13.913 --> 00:29:15.710
This is Captain Janeway
on Voyager.

00:29:15.749 --> 00:29:17.478
I urge you
to break off your attack.

00:29:17.517 --> 00:29:19.451
One of my crew members
is aboard the missile.

00:29:19.486 --> 00:29:21.147
You'd better get
your crewman out, Captain.

00:29:21.187 --> 00:29:23.553
We estimate time to intercept,
90 seconds.

00:29:23.590 --> 00:29:25.319
We're still attempting
to disarm its weapons.

00:29:25.358 --> 00:29:26.916
My orders are clear.

00:29:26.993 --> 00:29:29.052
You'll have to talk
to my superiors back home.

00:29:29.095 --> 00:29:30.392
Rakosa One, out.

00:29:30.430 --> 00:29:31.397
Janeway to Torres.

00:29:31.431 --> 00:29:32.398
Yes, Captain.

00:29:32.432 --> 00:29:34.229
The Rakosan fleet
is preparing to attack.

00:29:34.267 --> 00:29:36.132
Captain, don't beam me out.

00:29:36.169 --> 00:29:38.137
I may not be able
to transport back here again.

00:29:38.171 --> 00:29:39.195
Lieutenant...

00:29:39.239 --> 00:29:40.297
I'm making progress!

00:29:40.340 --> 00:29:42.706
The Rakosan ships
have created a diversion.

00:29:42.742 --> 00:29:45.802
I've already used it to disarm
the security codes on board.

00:29:45.845 --> 00:29:47.676
Now if I can just get
to the central processor,

00:29:47.714 --> 00:29:49.614
I can disable the entire system.

00:29:49.649 --> 00:29:50.616
All right.

00:29:50.650 --> 00:29:52.117
We'll try to keep
a transporter lock on you.

00:29:52.152 --> 00:29:53.312
Janeway out.

00:29:53.353 --> 00:29:55.412
The Rakosan attack
is commencing, Captain.

00:29:55.455 --> 00:29:57.616
Move us into weapons range,
Mr. Paris.

00:29:57.657 --> 00:29:58.783
Aye, Captain.

00:29:58.825 --> 00:30:00.816
Give them some cover fire.
Red Alert.

00:30:01.961 --> 00:30:04.589
Firing phasers.

00:30:21.181 --> 00:30:24.673
All command control functions
have been rerouted

00:30:24.718 --> 00:30:27.209
through protected
backup circuits, B'Elanna.

00:30:27.253 --> 00:30:29.847
Your attempt to compromise
weapons control

00:30:29.889 --> 00:30:31.356
has been blocked.

00:30:31.391 --> 00:30:34.155
Those ships aren't your enemy.

00:30:34.194 --> 00:30:36.321
They are not Cardassian.

00:30:36.362 --> 00:30:38.296
Can't you recognize that?

00:30:38.331 --> 00:30:39.559
This vessel is programmed

00:30:39.599 --> 00:30:41.590
to respond
with all necessary force

00:30:41.634 --> 00:30:44.102
to prevent any disruption
to its mission.

00:30:56.850 --> 00:30:58.317
Shields are holding.

00:30:58.351 --> 00:31:00.581
We are drawing minimal fire
from the missile.

00:31:00.620 --> 00:31:01.882
Its primary weapon systems

00:31:01.921 --> 00:31:03.354
are focused
on the Rakosan vessel.

00:31:03.389 --> 00:31:06.324
Another group of fighters
is starting an attack run.

00:31:06.359 --> 00:31:07.849
We've got to draw more
of the missile's fire.

00:31:07.894 --> 00:31:11.125
Make Voyager
a more serious threat, Tuvok.

00:31:15.034 --> 00:31:17.332
Shields at 40 percent.

00:31:17.370 --> 00:31:19.634
Damage reported
on Decks 3 and 4.

00:31:19.672 --> 00:31:20.696
Repair crews responding.

00:31:20.740 --> 00:31:23.971
The Rakosan vessels
are withdrawing, Captain.

00:31:24.010 --> 00:31:26.342
Good. Move us out of range
of the plasma wave.

00:31:26.379 --> 00:31:27.368
Janeway to Torres.

00:31:27.413 --> 00:31:28.380
Yes, Captain.

00:31:28.414 --> 00:31:29.904
The Rakosan ships
have retreated.

00:31:29.949 --> 00:31:31.280
We have one hour
and nine minutes

00:31:31.317 --> 00:31:32.545
until the missile
reaches the planet.

00:31:32.585 --> 00:31:33.745
Any progress?

00:31:33.787 --> 00:31:35.846
Dreadnought's created
backup systems

00:31:35.889 --> 00:31:38.153
to replace the ones
I tried to disable.

00:31:38.191 --> 00:31:39.920
Do you have any other ideas?

00:31:39.959 --> 00:31:42.826
I'm reluctant to discuss them
in present company,

00:31:42.862 --> 00:31:44.022
but could you send over a?

00:31:47.734 --> 00:31:49.964
Captain?

00:31:50.003 --> 00:31:52.403
Communications
have been terminated.

00:31:52.438 --> 00:31:55.168
Transporter lock
has also been disengaged.

00:31:55.208 --> 00:31:57.676
What took you so long?

00:31:57.710 --> 00:31:59.405
There was a tactical advantage

00:31:59.445 --> 00:32:01.640
in monitoring
your ship's communications

00:32:01.681 --> 00:32:03.876
until this time.

00:32:03.917 --> 00:32:06.477
So...

00:32:06.519 --> 00:32:09.420
it's just you and me now.

00:32:19.899 --> 00:32:22.629
You are accessing
the detonation control circuit.

00:32:22.669 --> 00:32:26.070
Probability assessment indicates
you are attempting to detonate

00:32:26.105 --> 00:32:29.165
the explosive
before it reaches its target.

00:32:29.209 --> 00:32:31.939
Now, that wouldn't make
much sense, would it?

00:32:31.978 --> 00:32:35.072
I'd be killing myself
in the process.

00:32:35.114 --> 00:32:38.140
Probability assessment indicates
you are attempting to detonate

00:32:38.184 --> 00:32:40.948
the explosive
before it reaches its target.

00:32:40.987 --> 00:32:44.081
If I'm being coerced
by Cardassians,

00:32:44.123 --> 00:32:46.751
why would I be willing
to sacrifice myself for them?

00:32:46.793 --> 00:32:48.590
Answer that one.

00:32:48.628 --> 00:32:51.859
Unable to respond.

00:32:51.898 --> 00:32:54.196
Reassessing probabilities.

00:32:54.234 --> 00:32:56.168
Aha.

00:32:56.202 --> 00:32:57.294
Gotcha.

00:32:58.771 --> 00:33:01.740
Why don't we reassess
those probabilities together?

00:33:01.774 --> 00:33:03.298
Okay?

00:33:03.343 --> 00:33:08.110
Remember how we used to play
hypothetical games?

00:33:08.147 --> 00:33:09.114
Affirmative.

00:33:09.148 --> 00:33:10.615
Let's play one now.

00:33:10.650 --> 00:33:13.244
Here's a hypothetical situation
for you.

00:33:13.286 --> 00:33:17.279
Suppose I've been telling you
the truth all along

00:33:17.323 --> 00:33:20.417
and you really are
in the Delta Quadrant...

00:33:20.460 --> 00:33:22.690
Probability of being
in the Delta Quadrant,

00:33:22.729 --> 00:33:25.630
75,000 light-years
from last confirmed location,

00:33:25.665 --> 00:33:26.757
is negligible.

00:33:26.799 --> 00:33:29.359
"Hypothetical," Dreadnought.
It's a game, remember?

00:33:29.402 --> 00:33:31.233
Assume it's true for a moment.

00:33:31.271 --> 00:33:32.329
Assumption entered.

00:33:32.372 --> 00:33:34.169
And we're heading
for the wrong target...

00:33:34.207 --> 00:33:35.640
Assumption entered.

00:33:35.675 --> 00:33:38.473
Millions of innocent people
about to die when you detonate.

00:33:38.511 --> 00:33:39.705
Assumption entered.

00:33:39.746 --> 00:33:42.909
Now explain to me
how this might happen.

00:33:42.949 --> 00:33:46.214
If key sensor programs
were damaged or deleted,

00:33:46.252 --> 00:33:48.379
data banks would be compromised.

00:33:49.555 --> 00:33:51.614
Just for the fun of it,

00:33:51.658 --> 00:33:54.559
let's have a look
at those data banks.

00:33:54.594 --> 00:33:58.826
See if anything looks at all...
"compromised."

00:34:03.102 --> 00:34:05.195
Is this
a complete file directory?

00:34:05.238 --> 00:34:06.865
There seem to be a few missing.

00:34:06.906 --> 00:34:08.931
Files containing information

00:34:09.008 --> 00:34:11.169
about the weapons
or tactical systems

00:34:11.210 --> 00:34:13.872
are not necessary
to verify sensor accuracy.

00:34:13.913 --> 00:34:14.880
Oh, I'm hurt.

00:34:14.914 --> 00:34:16.074
You don't trust me.

00:34:17.483 --> 00:34:18.541
Hold on.

00:34:18.584 --> 00:34:20.279
Pause the display.

00:34:20.320 --> 00:34:22.845
What's that?

00:34:22.889 --> 00:34:25.619
Computer, identify
the Cardassian file on screen.

00:34:25.658 --> 00:34:28.388
Unable to identify.

00:34:28.428 --> 00:34:31.488
It looks like a backup file.

00:34:31.531 --> 00:34:34.864
Computer,
when was this file created?

00:34:34.901 --> 00:34:38.837
Stardate 46437.5.

00:34:38.871 --> 00:34:42.307
I believe that was
before you and I ever met.

00:34:42.440 --> 00:34:44.704
Hypothetical game terminated.

00:34:44.742 --> 00:34:46.869
Probability reassessment
complete.

00:34:46.911 --> 00:34:47.878
A new conclusion?

00:34:47.912 --> 00:34:49.140
Affirmative.

00:34:49.180 --> 00:34:51.648
Probability of being
in the Delta Quadrant

00:34:51.683 --> 00:34:52.775
remains negligible.

00:34:52.817 --> 00:34:54.512
When that option is rejected,

00:34:54.552 --> 00:34:56.281
new probability assessment
indicates

00:34:56.321 --> 00:34:58.380
that you have changed loyalties,
B'Elanna.

00:34:58.423 --> 00:35:01.449
You are now cooperating with the
Cardassian-Federation Alliance,

00:35:01.492 --> 00:35:04.620
as described
in the treaty of 2367,

00:35:04.662 --> 00:35:06.357
a treaty which has been rejected
by the Maquis.

00:35:06.397 --> 00:35:07.864
Dreadnought...

00:35:07.899 --> 00:35:10.367
Humanoid life support
aboard this vessel

00:35:10.401 --> 00:35:11.732
has been terminated.

00:35:11.769 --> 00:35:13.862
Approaching target
at full impulse.

00:35:13.905 --> 00:35:16.738
Stage one alert
has been activated.

00:35:16.774 --> 00:35:20.005
Initiating
final detonation sequence.

00:35:26.617 --> 00:35:28.084
People are crowding every port

00:35:28.119 --> 00:35:30.110
trying to get off
the eastern continent.

00:35:30.154 --> 00:35:31.553
There aren't enough ships.

00:35:31.589 --> 00:35:35.616
Kellan, there are still 41
minutes for us to prevent this.

00:35:35.660 --> 00:35:37.594
What can be done in 41 minutes?

00:35:42.633 --> 00:35:45.602
I'm prepared to use this ship
to detonate the warhead

00:35:45.636 --> 00:35:47.968
before the missile reaches you.

00:35:48.039 --> 00:35:49.529
Use your ship?

00:35:51.709 --> 00:35:52.733
To collide with it?

00:35:52.777 --> 00:35:54.574
Something like that.

00:35:54.612 --> 00:35:57.775
Do you really think
that would work?

00:35:57.815 --> 00:35:59.976
I'm not sure.

00:36:00.051 --> 00:36:02.417
You would sacrifice yourselves

00:36:02.453 --> 00:36:06.253
to benefit a people you didn't
even know two days ago?

00:36:06.290 --> 00:36:09.282
To save two million lives?

00:36:09.327 --> 00:36:11.318
That's not a hard decision.

00:36:11.362 --> 00:36:16.197
Your reputation in this Quadrant
isn't deserved, Captain.

00:36:17.468 --> 00:36:20.198
For what it's worth...

00:36:20.238 --> 00:36:22.297
you've made a friend here.

00:36:22.340 --> 00:36:24.535
I'm still hoping
we'll have a chance

00:36:24.575 --> 00:36:26.975
to celebrate
this new friendship together.

00:36:29.981 --> 00:36:31.676
All key systems
have been secured.

00:36:31.716 --> 00:36:34.378
You will not gain access.

00:36:34.419 --> 00:36:38.253
I'm not interested in your key
systems anymore, Dreadnought.

00:36:38.289 --> 00:36:41.315
That is an unlikely assertion,
B'Elanna.

00:36:41.359 --> 00:36:42.883
Seriously.

00:36:42.927 --> 00:36:44.394
Check for yourself.

00:36:55.873 --> 00:36:58.967
You are attempting to access
the obsolete Cardassian file.

00:36:59.076 --> 00:37:00.270
Why?

00:37:00.311 --> 00:37:02.711
Oh, just killing time.

00:37:02.747 --> 00:37:05.045
Life support
has been terminated.

00:37:05.082 --> 00:37:08.017
It is advisable for you
to return to your ship.

00:37:16.394 --> 00:37:19.557
Gentlemen,
I believe our best chance

00:37:19.597 --> 00:37:21.895
at stopping Dreadnought now
is to set off

00:37:21.933 --> 00:37:25.300
a large antimatter explosion
directly in its path.

00:37:25.336 --> 00:37:26.803
To work, it would
take more energy

00:37:26.838 --> 00:37:28.362
than all our photons
put together.

00:37:28.406 --> 00:37:29.930
Or more to the point,

00:37:29.974 --> 00:37:32.135
it would take
a warp core breach.

00:37:33.778 --> 00:37:36.269
You'll be in charge
of the evacuation, Commander.

00:37:36.314 --> 00:37:38.908
I'm not leaving you
on this ship.

00:37:38.950 --> 00:37:40.747
Captain's prerogative.

00:37:40.785 --> 00:37:42.480
Get the rest of the crew
to the escape pods.

00:37:42.520 --> 00:37:44.784
I'll send the senior officers
to join you in a few minutes.

00:37:44.822 --> 00:37:47.518
We don't have time
to debate this, Chakotay.

00:37:51.762 --> 00:37:54.697
Everyone except senior officers,
with me.

00:37:56.467 --> 00:38:00.267
Computer, initiate
the self-destruct sequence.

00:38:00.304 --> 00:38:03.535
Authorization:
Janeway-pi-one-one-zero.

00:38:03.574 --> 00:38:05.132
Set it at 20 minutes.

00:38:05.176 --> 00:38:08.907
Warning. Self-destruct sequence
has been initiated.

00:38:09.013 --> 00:38:11.208
Warp core overload
in 20 minutes.

00:38:15.820 --> 00:38:19.187
Cardassian A-T-R 4-1-0-7.

00:38:19.223 --> 00:38:21.691
Attempting to activate systems.

00:38:21.726 --> 00:38:24.854
I never thought I'd be glad
to hear that voice again.

00:38:24.896 --> 00:38:28.593
Voice analyzer functioning.
Unable to identify.

00:38:28.633 --> 00:38:30.692
Attempting to activate systems.

00:38:30.735 --> 00:38:32.669
No additional presence detected.

00:38:32.703 --> 00:38:35.365
Check those diagnostics,
Dreadnought.

00:38:35.406 --> 00:38:36.566
You're talking to yourself.

00:38:36.607 --> 00:38:41.101
I believe you're having
an identity crisis.

00:38:41.145 --> 00:38:43.477
Accessing
central processor memory.

00:38:43.514 --> 00:38:46.244
Engaging counter-virus
response program.

00:38:46.284 --> 00:38:48.844
Attempting to override program.

00:38:50.488 --> 00:38:52.251
Computer...

00:38:52.290 --> 00:38:56.090
identify the target.

00:38:56.127 --> 00:38:57.617
The Maquis munitions...

00:38:57.662 --> 00:38:59.960
The Cardassian fuel depot
on Aschelan V.

00:39:00.031 --> 00:39:03.159
Malfunction detected
in the targeting system.

00:39:03.200 --> 00:39:04.565
Attempting to correct.

00:39:04.602 --> 00:39:05.899
Negative.

00:39:06.003 --> 00:39:07.732
Target lock has been confirmed.

00:39:07.772 --> 00:39:09.569
The Maquis are now in control...

00:39:09.607 --> 00:39:10.904
This target does not conform

00:39:10.975 --> 00:39:12.408
to established
targeting parameters.

00:39:12.443 --> 00:39:14.604
The original targeting
parameters have been replaced...

00:39:14.645 --> 00:39:16.579
The detonation sequence
cannot proceed without...

00:39:16.614 --> 00:39:18.809
The countdown to the detonation
sequence will continue.

00:39:18.849 --> 00:39:19.907
Ejecting antimatter pods.

00:39:20.017 --> 00:39:21.416
Aschelan V will be destroyed.

00:39:21.452 --> 00:39:23.113
The emergency ejection system
has failed.

00:39:23.154 --> 00:39:25.622
Attempting to reinitialize
all key circuits.

00:39:25.656 --> 00:39:27.681
Access to the navigational
system is denied.

00:39:27.725 --> 00:39:28.919
Accessing backup system.

00:39:28.993 --> 00:39:30.187
All critical pathways

00:39:30.227 --> 00:39:31.922
have been rerouted
to protected backup systems.

00:39:31.963 --> 00:39:33.828
Security lockouts functioning...

00:39:53.918 --> 00:39:55.078
Yes.

00:40:10.735 --> 00:40:14.762
Warning. Self-destruct sequence
has been initiated.

00:40:14.805 --> 00:40:16.773
Warp core overload
in 11 minutes.

00:40:16.807 --> 00:40:20.140
Captain, I've broken
through the interference.

00:40:20.177 --> 00:40:21.644
I'm not sure how.

00:40:21.679 --> 00:40:23.306
We have communications.

00:40:23.347 --> 00:40:25.508
Checking on
transporter signal.

00:40:25.549 --> 00:40:26.982
I have a lock on her.

00:40:27.018 --> 00:40:27.985
Voyager to Torres.

00:40:28.019 --> 00:40:28.986
Yes, Captain.

00:40:29.020 --> 00:40:30.180
I need to get you out of there.

00:40:30.221 --> 00:40:31.279
We're abandoning Voyager.

00:40:31.322 --> 00:40:32.448
I'm going to overload

00:40:32.490 --> 00:40:34.355
the warp core
in the missile's flight path.

00:40:34.392 --> 00:40:36.917
I may be able to detonate
the warhead from here

00:40:36.961 --> 00:40:39.088
by breaching
the containment field.

00:40:39.130 --> 00:40:40.597
Can you get access to the core?

00:40:40.631 --> 00:40:41.962
I'm already in it.

00:40:41.999 --> 00:40:43.398
I'm using my phaser

00:40:43.434 --> 00:40:46.665
to burn through the magnetic
constrictor casing now.

00:40:48.572 --> 00:40:51.234
Are you all right, B'Elanna?

00:40:51.275 --> 00:40:52.833
Fine.

00:40:52.877 --> 00:40:55.141
The air's just
a little thin in here.

00:40:55.179 --> 00:40:56.168
Keep me advised.

00:40:56.213 --> 00:40:57.840
Janeway out.

00:40:57.882 --> 00:41:01.374
Mr. Kim,
transfer control to the Conn

00:41:01.419 --> 00:41:02.943
and report to your escape pod.

00:41:03.020 --> 00:41:04.749
Captain...

00:41:04.789 --> 00:41:06.518
That's a direct order
to all of you.

00:41:06.557 --> 00:41:08.354
Mr. Paris, I'm relieving you.

00:41:08.392 --> 00:41:09.518
Now!

00:41:13.130 --> 00:41:14.495
The starboard thrusters
are a little sluggish.

00:41:14.532 --> 00:41:15.931
Ease into them.

00:41:15.966 --> 00:41:17.166
Understood.

00:41:19.801 --> 00:41:21.291
Captain...

00:41:22.804 --> 00:41:24.738
thanks for everything.

00:41:26.575 --> 00:41:30.705
Warning. Self-destruct sequence
has been initiated.

00:41:30.746 --> 00:41:33.544
Warp core overload
in seven minutes.

00:41:33.582 --> 00:41:35.413
You, too, Tuvok.

00:41:35.450 --> 00:41:39.250
It is logical to have
a second-in-command

00:41:39.288 --> 00:41:40.277
in case you are injured

00:41:40.322 --> 00:41:42.222
and unable to complete
the mission, Captain.

00:41:42.257 --> 00:41:44.248
I request permission
to remain.

00:41:46.161 --> 00:41:47.753
Permission granted.

00:41:56.672 --> 00:41:57.969
Hello, B'Elanna.

00:41:58.006 --> 00:42:00.941
The Cardassian virus
has been neutralized.

00:42:00.976 --> 00:42:02.944
Good for you.

00:42:03.045 --> 00:42:05.878
Containment field integrity
at 40 percent

00:42:05.914 --> 00:42:07.575
and falling.

00:42:07.616 --> 00:42:11.746
Estimated time to breach.

00:42:11.787 --> 00:42:15.553
This vessel is programmed to
respond with all necessary force

00:42:15.591 --> 00:42:18.389
to prevent any disruption
to its mission.

00:42:18.427 --> 00:42:20.258
Unless I'm mistaken,

00:42:20.295 --> 00:42:23.492
you're out of options,
Dreadnought.

00:42:23.532 --> 00:42:26.330
Analysis of your vital signs
suggests

00:42:26.368 --> 00:42:28.461
you are about to lose
consciousness, B'Elanna.

00:42:28.503 --> 00:42:33.202
I'm not going anywhere
until I'm finished.

00:42:33.242 --> 00:42:36.268
When you cease your efforts
to breach the containment field,

00:42:36.311 --> 00:42:38.711
life support will be restored.

00:42:38.747 --> 00:42:40.681
No deal.

00:42:40.716 --> 00:42:44.482
Warning. Self-destruct sequence
has been initiated.

00:42:44.519 --> 00:42:46.282
Warp core overload
in three minutes.

00:42:46.321 --> 00:42:47.652
Increasing velocity.

00:42:47.689 --> 00:42:50.749
Preparing to adjust our heading
to intercept.

00:42:52.361 --> 00:42:54.124
Janeway to Torres.

00:42:54.162 --> 00:42:55.823
Yes?

00:42:55.864 --> 00:42:58.890
This is your last chance
to get back here, B'Elanna.

00:42:58.934 --> 00:43:00.834
I have to launch
the last escape pods.

00:43:02.537 --> 00:43:03.936
I understand, Captain.

00:43:03.972 --> 00:43:06.736
I'm almost finished.

00:43:06.775 --> 00:43:08.606
Let me stay.

00:43:08.644 --> 00:43:11.772
Warning. Self-destruct sequence
has been initiated.

00:43:11.813 --> 00:43:13.940
Warp core overload
in two minutes.

00:43:14.049 --> 00:43:18.179
Containment field integrity
at 20 percent and falling.

00:43:18.220 --> 00:43:21.781
Perhaps your Delta Quadrant
hypothesis

00:43:21.823 --> 00:43:23.450
deserves further consideration.

00:43:25.294 --> 00:43:27.285
Nice try.

00:43:29.665 --> 00:43:32.828
Who would have thought
two years ago,

00:43:32.868 --> 00:43:36.736
after all those weeks
we spent together

00:43:36.772 --> 00:43:38.603
perfecting your program...

00:43:40.809 --> 00:43:43.642
that we'd end up out here...

00:43:43.679 --> 00:43:46.307
trying to kill each other.

00:43:46.348 --> 00:43:51.980
Probability assessment did not
anticipate this outcome.

00:43:52.087 --> 00:43:53.611
The missile's containment
field is collapsing.

00:43:53.655 --> 00:43:56.089
Beam her back now.
Hang on.

00:44:00.128 --> 00:44:03.564
Warning. Self-destruct sequence
has been initiated.

00:44:03.598 --> 00:44:05.793
Warp core overload
in one minute.

00:44:05.834 --> 00:44:07.768
Computer, terminate
self-destruct sequence.

00:44:07.803 --> 00:44:10.363
Authorization:
Janeway-pi-one-one-zero.

00:44:10.405 --> 00:44:12.839
Confirmed.
Sequence terminated.

00:44:12.874 --> 00:44:14.637
Janeway to Torres.
B'Elanna, are you?

00:44:14.676 --> 00:44:16.871
She's here in Sick Bay, Captain.

00:44:16.912 --> 00:44:19.847
Please turn to your emergency
medical holographic channel.

00:44:19.881 --> 00:44:21.940
Doctor, I forgot about you.

00:44:22.017 --> 00:44:24.645
How flattering.
I wanted to advise you

00:44:24.686 --> 00:44:27.120
that I took the liberty
of beaming Lieutenant Torres

00:44:27.155 --> 00:44:29.089
from the transporter room
to Sick Bay.

00:44:29.124 --> 00:44:31.183
She is somewhat singed
around the edges,

00:44:31.226 --> 00:44:33.820
but should make
a complete recovery.

00:44:33.862 --> 00:44:35.887
Very good, Doctor.

00:44:35.931 --> 00:44:37.296
Janeway out.

00:44:38.867 --> 00:44:42.963
Mr. Tuvok, prepare to retrieve
our escape pods.

00:44:43.071 --> 00:44:44.902
Let's bring our crew home.

00:44:44.940 --> 00:44:46.635
Aye, Captain.
